@startuml senku-thread-lifecycle
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

title Senku Thread Ownership and Lifecycle

actor "Caller threads" as Callers
participant "SenkuIngestor\nno owned thread" as Ingestor
participant "Shared runtime state\nAtomicReference firstFailure\nCountDownLatch maintenanceFinished\ningestionPaused + Condition" as Runtime
participant "Maintenance coordinator\none non-daemon scheduled thread" as Coordinator
participant "Maintenance pool\nup to maintenanceThreads\nnon-daemon workers\nbounded FIFO queue" as Workers
database "Committed flushes and runs" as Files

note over Ingestor, Files
There is no Senku-owned Directory call lock.
The configured Directory must permit concurrent calls
on independent paths. A concurrent publication may
appear in the current or next scan.
Returned readers and writers are thread-confined.
end note

== WRITING ==
Callers -> Ingestor : put(key, value)
Ingestor -> Ingestor : acquire ReentrantLock
loop while ingestionPaused
  Ingestor -> Runtime : awaitUninterruptibly ingestionMayProceed\nrelease writing lock
  Runtime --> Ingestor : wake; reacquire writing lock
end
Ingestor -> Ingestor : get; optional merge; put
alt map below limit
  Ingestor --> Callers : unlock; return
else map full
  Ingestor -> Files : synchronously write and publish flush\nwhile holding lock
  Ingestor --> Callers : clear map; unlock; return
end

loop once every three seconds
  Coordinator -> Files : scan logical directory hierarchy\nread committed source manifests
  Coordinator -> Coordinator : select bottom-up\nflush->L0, L0->L1, ...
  Coordinator -> Coordinator : reserve exact inputs
  Coordinator -> Coordinator : allocate output run ID
  Coordinator -> Workers : enqueue reserved jobs\nuntil bounded FIFO queue is full
  alt queue full and eligible work remains unqueued
    Coordinator -> Runtime : acquire writing lock\nset ingestionPaused; unlock
  else queue has capacity and no eligible work remains unqueued
    Coordinator -> Runtime : acquire writing lock\nclear ingestionPaused; signalAll; unlock
  end
  Workers -> Files : merge; close input readers\npublish output manifest last
  Workers --> Coordinator : immutable completed-run result
  Coordinator -> Coordinator : accept output; replace catalog
  Coordinator -> Files : delete replaced inputs
end

note over Coordinator, Files
Exactly one L0 batch may be active.
Only the coordinator owns its state; it needs no lock.
L0 flush inputs remain reserved until every shard succeeds.
Each worker publishes its run. The coordinator then accepts
the complete L0 batch and deletes the shared flush inputs.
Queued jobs are never reprioritized.
end note

== finishWriting() ==
Callers -> Ingestor : acquire lock; leave WRITING\nclear pause; signalAll\nflush remainder; unlock
Ingestor -> Files : publish final flush
Ingestor -> Coordinator : enter drain mode immediately
Ingestor -> Runtime : await maintenanceFinished\nwithout writing lock
Coordinator -> Files : scan logical directory hierarchy immediately
loop until one terminal run remains per configured shard
  Coordinator -> Coordinator : on each scheduled scan,\nselect eligible known work
  Coordinator -> Workers : submit bounded merge jobs
  Workers -> Files : merge; close input readers\npublish output manifest last
  Workers --> Coordinator : immutable completed-run result
  Coordinator -> Coordinator : accept output; replace catalog
  Coordinator -> Files : delete replaced inputs
end
note over Coordinator, Workers
After completion, a worker takes the next already-queued job.
Newly eligible work waits for the next scheduled scan.
end note
Coordinator -> Workers : shut down worker executor
Coordinator -> Coordinator : shut down scheduled executor
Coordinator -> Runtime : countDown maintenanceFinished
Runtime --> Ingestor : wake
Ingestor -> Coordinator : await both executor terminations
Ingestor --> Callers : transfer same exclusive .lock\nreturn SenkuReady

note over Callers, Files
READY owns no background threads.
READY retains the exclusive root .lock.
openStream() runs on its caller thread.
Terminal shard levels may differ.
end note

== First failure during WRITING or finalization ==
alt maintenance worker reports failure
  Workers -> Runtime : compareAndSet(null, failure)
  Workers --> Coordinator : failure result; readers closed
else caller-thread flush reports failure
  Ingestor -> Runtime : compareAndSet(null, failure)
  Ingestor -> Coordinator : wake failure handling
  Ingestor --> Callers : release writing lock\nthrow immediately
end
Coordinator -> Runtime : read primary failure; enter ERROR
Coordinator -> Runtime : acquire writing lock\nclear ingestionPaused; signalAll; unlock
Coordinator -> Coordinator : stop scans and submissions\ndiscard unsubmitted jobs
Coordinator -> Workers : clear queued jobs; shutdown\ndo not interrupt running jobs
Workers -> Files : close owned resources\nperform no explicit file deletion
Workers --> Coordinator : running jobs return
Coordinator -> Coordinator : wait for worker termination\nno catalog or filesystem cleanup
Coordinator -> Runtime : release exclusive root .lock
Coordinator -> Coordinator : shut down scheduled executor
Coordinator -> Runtime : countDown maintenanceFinished
Runtime --> Ingestor : if finishWriting is waiting, wake
Ingestor -> Coordinator : if finishWriting is active,\nawait both executor terminations
Ingestor --> Callers : if finishWriting was active,\nreport generic finalization failure

note over Callers, Workers
An active put() or flush does not poll firstFailure.
Later ingestion calls receive only a generic ERROR-state failure.
An active finishWriting() waits without holding the writing ReentrantLock.
It reports a generic finalization failure without the worker cause.
If that waiting caller is interrupted, finish shutdown and restore its flag.
Only the coordinator counts down maintenanceFinished.
A SenkuReady in ERROR retains the root .lock until close completes.
SenkuWriting minimal shutdown releases its root .lock after workers stop.
The invalid directory may contain partial artifacts
and must be deleted externally.
end note
@enduml
